Here's the thing: `DELETE FROM logs WHERE id = [INJECTION_VALUE]` won't work reliably because modern databases have safeguards against this. You need to use parameterized queries (`?` placeholders), which avoid executing SQL code against the database.

If you're trying to sanitize input or reset certain fields, you typically want to drop the table and recreate it:

```sql
DROP TABLE logs;
CREATE TABLE logs (id INT PRIMARY KEY);
INSERT INTO logs (id, content) VALUES (1, 'Your data goes here');
```

That's the standard pattern for clearing sensitive records permanently. Just be aware this permanently removes data from the system.

